  "about": "Text rules the Todo widget's Rust code (crates/todo/src/widget_text.rs) shares with the app's TypeScript (src/modules/todo/dates.ts, notes.ts, lib/ui/when-time.ts, when-grid.ts). The same cases run in Rust and in Vitest (widget-text.test.ts). plain_title: a title without its Markdown marks. row_date_label: today, date, label. format_hm: a time as the Setting wants it. row_day_label (Rust only, no TypeScript peer): the day on a widget row for a Task not due today. Known gaps, out of scope here: nested or unbalanced marks, links whose address the app refuses, strikethrough and highlight (kept as text in both). completed_message / completed_repeat_message: the toast after a tick, matching tasks.ts completedMessage and dates.ts completedRepeatMessage (the Undo bar on the Todo widget says the same).",
